# Agent framework coexistence

BellLabs is both a biotech research/ingestion/evaluation service and a frontier agent-framework/model evaluation service.

- Keep BellLabs shared contracts, domain invariants, provenance, budgets, approvals, ingestion gates, and durable lifecycle state authoritative and framework-neutral.
- Treat agent frameworks and model providers as execution adapters, not domain authorities. Do not leak provider SDK objects or ambiguous provider IDs into shared contracts.
- Use LangChain/LangGraph/Deep Agents/LangSmith behind BellLabs ports and exact run bindings for the
  accepted target. `WP-CP-040` removed the OpenAI Agents SDK runtime and dependency; do not
  reintroduce it, a compatibility path, or a provider fallback without a new accepted package and
  qualification. Direct model APIs remain eligible only through explicitly accepted adapters.
- Do not force a least-common-denominator runtime. Model shared semantics in the core contracts and express special capabilities through explicit, provider-qualified capability profiles and adapters.
- Current delivery priority: Temporal is the sole macro runtime and Deep Agents is bounded
  operation cognition. Agent Server may host bounded operation, qualification, development, and
  shared assets; it is not a production family scheduler.
- Comparable provider-native runtimes are future architecture/evaluation work, not current
  implementation authority.
- Treat the hypothesis that provider-native models perform better with provider-native agent tooling as something to measure, not assume.
- Compare quality, citation fidelity, ingestion correctness, safety, latency, cost, durability, observability, intervention, and recovery using frozen inputs, budgets, outputs, and evaluator versions.
- Select a runtime per exact Workflow Implementation or operation binding; never create multiple authorities for one BellLabs run or allow runtime state to bypass admission and settlement.
- Preserve the distinction between researched evidence and approved ingestion. No framework may write canonical knowledge without BellLabs validation, provenance, policy, and review gates.

